free interest rate is based on the yields of United&nbsp;States Treasury securities with maturities similar to the expected life of the share options
in effect at the time of&nbsp;grant. </FONT></DD><DT style='font-family:times;margin-bottom:-11pt;'><FONT SIZE=2>(ii)</FONT></DT><DD style="font-family:times;"><FONT SIZE=2>Expected
dividend is assumed to be 0% as the Company has no history or expectation of paying a dividend on its ordinary shares.  </FONT></DD><DT style='font-family:times;margin-bottom:-11pt;'><FONT SIZE=2>(iii)</FONT></DT><DD style="font-family:times;"><FONT SIZE=2>Expected
life of share options is based on the average between the vesting period and the contractual term for each&nbsp;grant. </FONT></DD><DT style='font-family:times;margin-bottom:-11pt;'><FONT SIZE=2>(iv)</FONT></DT><DD style="font-family:times;"><FONT SIZE=2>Expected
volatility is assumed based on the historical volatility of the Company's comparable companies in the period equal to the expected life of
each&nbsp;grant.  </FONT></DD></DL>
</UL>
